      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T13:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`excluded{Path,File}` are the result of calling `excludedPath():L828` and `excludedFile():L819`.\n\n`excludedPath`, for instance, would extract the text after `-path`\n\n```\nPattern.compile(\".*-path:([^ ]*).*\")\n```\n\nSo it would return: `^Jenkinsfile$`\n\nHere we compare that text literally in `file.equals(excludedPath)`, so it will be something like:\n\n```\n\"Jenkinsfile\".equals(\"^Jenkinsfile$\")\n```\n\nWhich is going to be `false`.\n\nThe same thing is true for the `file` path.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 704,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 705,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "244bf5fe241eb3845154dd5527608aab5f54e89b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
