      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T13:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure this is going to work.\n\nTake for example, `-file:src`.\n\nAs per the docs, in Gerrit, this would mean: \"exclude a change if it touches a path component named `src`\".\n\nSo, for example:\n\n```\nsrc/Main.java\nsrc/main/java/App.java\nplugins/foo/src/test/java/AppTest.java\n```\n\nSo imagine we have set the exclusion filter to be `-file:src` and we have a chain of changes like this:\n\n```\nTarget branch\n  └─ Change A: modifies src/main/java/App.java\n       └─ Change B: modifies README.md\n```\n\nHere, when we do `file.endsWith(\"/\" + excludedFile)` we will return `false` because it does not end with \"/src\", so we won\u0027t notice that Change A should have been excluded.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 706,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 706,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "244bf5fe241eb3845154dd5527608aab5f54e89b",
