      "message": "I think these extractors are a bit fragile.\nFor example, the administrator might configure:\n\n1. `-path:Jenkinsfile -path:ci/pipeline`\n\nSince `excludedPathPattern` is greedy, it would capture only `ci/pipeline`\n\n2. -path:\"Jenkinsfile\"\n\nWill extract `\"Jenkinsfile\"`, including quotes.\n\nCan we cover some scenarios in `AbstractGerritSCMSourceTest`, to understand how these (and other cases) would behave?",
